  {
   "id": "concept2",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Reflexive, symmetric, transitive"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "A relation $R$ on $A$ is reflexive if $(a, a) \\in R$ for every $a \\in A$; symmetric if $(a, b) \\in R$ implies $(b, a) \\in R$; transitive if $(a, b) \\in R$ and $(b, c) \\in R$ together imply $(a, c) \\in R$.",
